---
import Journal from '../layouts/Journal.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Journal
  title="About this edition"
  description="A fictional independent journal demonstrating Una Moderno's shared editorial layout in Astro."
  current="about"
  art="desktop-garden"
>
  <div class="una-layout">
    <main id="main" class="una-main" tabindex="-1">
      <article class="una-feature">
        <h1 class="una-title">A journal made to travel.</h1>
        <p class="una-deck">Different tools. The same editorial bones.</p>
        <div class="una-prose">
          <h2 id="this-edition">About this edition</h2>
          <p>
            These are demonstration stories. Dino Latoga is the lead-story byline; other
            contributors are fictional. The articles, geometric illustrations, and layout were
            created for Una Moderno, a portable editorial layout system for the independent web.
          </p>
          <p>
            This reference renders the same public specimen content through Astro. The stories live
            in this repository, so the example can be built without an account, a CMS, or private
            material.
          </p>
          <h2 id="art-and-type">Art and type</h2>
          <p>
            The story illustrations are original vector artwork created for this public project. The
            optional panoramic backgrounds were generated for Una Moderno under Dino’s direction and
            approved for this specimen. <a href="https://rsms.me/inter/">Inter</a>, released under
            the SIL Open Font License, supplies every text role. Light display type and regular
            reading text share one locally hosted variable face. Weight and scale establish
            hierarchy; system fonts keep the page readable if it cannot load.
          </p>
          <h2 id="design-inspiration">Design inspiration</h2>
          <p>
            The collection layout takes cues from Zune 4.0's typography and browsing rhythm. Una
            Moderno is an independent editorial project, unaffiliated with Microsoft. No Zune
            images, logos, or proprietary fonts are included.{' '}
            <a href="https://github.com/dinolatoga/una-moderno/blob/main/docs/zune-inspiration.md">
              Read the Zune inspiration and asset policy.
            </a>
          </p>
          <h2 id="room-for-words">Room for words</h2>
          <p>
            Artwork is optional. The{' '}
            <a href={`${base}no-image/`}>
              edition of “An archive of ordinary days” without an image
            </a>{' '}
            shows how the story holds its place when only the words remain.
          </p>
          <h2 id="origin">Where it began</h2>
          <p>
            Una Moderno descends from Dino Latoga's Una WordPress theme of 2008. The modern system
            keeps its editorial proportions and useful sidebar, while its core is ordinary HTML and
            CSS.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="https://github.com/dinolatoga/una-moderno">
              Read the project documentation and provenance on GitHub
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>
    <aside class="una-sidebar" aria-label="About this journal">
      <section class="una-module una-module--blue">
        <h2>start with a story</h2>
        <p>A place to read, follow a useful link, and find something worth keeping.</p>
        <p>
          <a href={base}>Back to the journal</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Journal>
